    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **276 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented digits-only telephone storage with normalization applied before the uniqueness check.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 relaxed the `telephone` request-validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted input like `(613) 555-0100` passes the `@Valid` DTO check instead of being rejected with a 400 before reaching the service.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 `setTelephone(...)` now strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"[^0-9]\", \"\")`), so the stored value \u2014 and thus the value returned in the `telephone` field on GET \u2014 is digits only. This produces exactly 10 digits, satisfying the entity's existing `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")`/`@Digits` constraints.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 the telephone-uniqueness check now uses a dedicated `normalizeTelephone(...)` helper that strips non-digits, so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` are treated as the same number and the duplicate is rejected with a 409.\n\nBoth cp11 tests pass (`coreStoresDigitsOnly` and `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`), and the whole existing suite remains green.",
